    [Attention][Feature] Support C8 MXFP8 KV cache quantization in Ascend v2 worker (#18485)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    This pull request implements support for C8 MXFP8 KV cache quantization
    in the Ascend v2 worker. Specifically, it:
    - Rewrites `FullAttentionSpec` to `mxfp_cache_spec` when MXFP8 KV
    quantization is enabled.
    - Implements `_reshape_kv_cache_v2` to build appropriate views for MXFP8
    caches.
    - Adds initialization and management of static V scale caches
    (`_fill_c8_mxfp_v_scale_caches`) and restores them during page
    reassignment in `update_requests`.
    - Integrates `AscendKVBlockZeroer` to handle zeroing of MXFP8 KV blocks
    while preserving static V scales.
    
    Feedback on this PR suggests adding defensive checks in
    `_fill_c8_mxfp_v_scale_caches` to avoid potential `ZeroDivisionError`
    and `IndexError` when `num_blocks` is 0 or `kv_cache` is malformed, as
    well as safely retrieving `static_forward_context` in
    `_init_kv_zero_meta` to prevent `AttributeError`.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    No, this is an internal enablement of MXFP8 KV cache quantization for
    Ascend NPU backends.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    New unit tests have been added in
    `tests/ut/worker/test_attn_utils_v2.py` and
    `tests/ut/worker/test_model_runner_v2.py` to verify the MXFP8 spec
    rewriting, cache reshaping, V-scale filling, and zeroing logic.
    
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/c4df37dfcc7f72ca41cd43801a468526ecf99a2b
    
    Signed-off-by: AJF-cmd <wangruiqing6@h-partners.com>

